    "body": "## Summary\n- harden Stripe refund webhook ordering when conflicting provider-resolved states share the same second-level `event.created`\n- move ambiguous local state to `REVIEW_REQUIRED` instead of letting webhook delivery order choose a financial outcome\n- preserve the last unambiguous provider observation and wallet reservation until a strictly newer signed event resolves the refund\n- add regression tests for same-second conflicts, newer-event recovery, and stale-event rejection\n- document the reconciliation rule in `docs/STRIPE_REFUNDS.md`\n\n## Financial safety\nA same-second conflict does not automatically restore reserved wallet funds and does not mark a competing provider outcome as authoritative. This prevents both duplicate-money restoration and silent local regression while retaining the existing rule that a genuinely newer Stripe failure can supersede an earlier success observation.\n\n## Validation\nCI required before merge: Maven verify, frontend test/lint/build, production Compose contract, runtime/container smoke, payments ledger smoke, platform fee settlement smoke, publication payment smoke, payout smoke where triggered.",
